sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: Conn plan O4 (Nick, 2026-11-14): Orbit pairs with a container T3 server on demand, holds the session, renews it, and hands it to the Node; the Node talks to the server directly. DECISIONS R1-R4. docs/reference/conn.md#held-sessions.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · API (conn-environment-session)
  %% kind: conn.session_hold
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane T3 icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>API callers
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant T3 as T3 server<br/>stock T3 auth API
  CLI->>GW: Read the held session<br/>GET conn/…/ENV/session
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `GET /api/v1/conn/environments/ENV/session`
  %%> - syntax: the MCP tool `conn-environment-session` with `environment`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the container Instance's T3 server; the calling Node is whose session it is
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - there is no `orbit` command; no pairing step on the device
  Note over GW: Check access, find session<br/>held pairing · Node · ENV
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the `conn` extension is on; the caller is an active Node
  %%> - the caller has an access grant to the Node that serves ENV, else `node_access.required`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a held session of the calling Node that has not ended answers at once (step 4); nothing else runs
  alt the Node holds a session
    GW-->>CLI: 200 OK · access_token<br/>url · expires_at
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - `environment_id`, `url`, `pairing_id`, `token_type: Bearer`, `access_token`, `expires_at`; `Cache-Control: no-store`
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the caller connects to `url` directly with the token as its bearer; the Gateway is not in that path
    %%> Why no task:
    %%> - a read of recorded state starts no run (R1); it takes about 0.1 s
  else no held session yet
    Note over GW: Record held pairing 7<br/>task #5172 · session to vault
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - ENV is a container Instance's server, else `conn.environment_not_instance`; not removing; not asleep, else `conn.environment_asleep`
    %%> - the Gateway's admin session on ENV has not ended, else `conn.session_expired`
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - takes ENV's row lock: an open hold of the same Node answers instead, so concurrent first reads start one task
    %%> - ignores `Idempotency-Key`: a repeated read answers the current state, never a replay
    %%> - records held pairing 7 with a unique label, such as `phone via Orbit k3j9x0qa`
    %%> - pushes the admin session to the Swamp vault after commit (R3)
    %%> Pre-mint:
    %%> - the same admission runs without a read when the switch `ORBIT_CONN_HELD_SESSION_PREMINT` is on (off by default) and the Gateway records a container server at the end of instance:create or instance:migrate: once for each Node of the creating Node's profile that reaches ENV
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-conn-session-hold
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the server URL, the label, T3's administrative scopes, and the vault key name; never a session
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5172
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the caller follows `GET /api/v1/conn/operations/5172` and reads the session again after success
  end
  Note over SW: Create private replies
  %%> How:
  %%> - mktemp creates a private directory for both T3 replies
  SW->>T3: Mint a pairing link<br/>POST /api/auth/pairing-token
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded curl from 209 with the admin session from `vault.get`, the label and the scopes
  Note over SW: Read the link
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - a typed data method reads T3's pairing result; the echoed label must match
  %%> - stores the one-time link as a native sensitive field; only its key name is public
  SW->>T3: Redeem the link<br/>POST /oauth/token
  %%> How:
  %%> - T3's normal pairing endpoint, as a device uses it: OAuth token exchange of the link, no DPoP proof
  %%> - curl reads the link from `vault.get` into a variable, never into argv
  %%> Why the Gateway can hand it on:
  %%> - T3 issues a plain bearer session; it checks only signature, end and revocation, not the client
  Note over SW: Store the session
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads T3's access-token result: a `Bearer` token, its scopes and `expires_in`
  %%> - stores the session as a native sensitive field and reports only public metadata
  Note over SW: Remove private replies
  %%> How:
  %%> - declared completed or skipped dependencies clean up after failure too
  Note over SW: Confirm session
  %%> Check:
  %%> - the native assert requires a stored session and successful cleanup
  alt T3 issued the session
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · expiry
    Note over GW: Keep the session<br/>encrypted · keys deleted
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the session key once, stores it encrypted on pairing 7, deletes the run's vault keys
    %%> - a revoke that named pairing 7 while it ran wins, whether it ended first or not: pairing 7 is withdrawn, never served, and revoked again by id
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5172 succeeds; its result holds only the pairing, link id and expiry
  else T3 refuses, answers badly or not at all
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>conn.* error_code
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - `conn.session_rejected`, `conn.request_refused`, `conn.response_invalid` or `conn.redeem_refused`: T3 answered, no session exists, the pairing is settled
    %%> - anything else is `conn.session_outcome_unknown`: the pairing is withdrawn and revoked by its label
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - the next read starts a new task with a new label
  end
  opt renewal (hourly, at wake)
    Note over GW: Renew under 7 days left<br/>renews_pairing_id
    %%> When:
    %%> - each held session that ends within seven days; also on Instances no device uses; a wake renews a sleeping Instance's
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the same run makes the new session; on success the old one is withdrawn and revoked by its pairing id
  end
